IMPORT prelude

-- Services Trust Funds Act 1947 (Cth) — THE NOUNS, THE RULES AND THE TOP-LEVEL
-- GOAL. Source: ../registers/source-bundle/C1947A00023.txt (compilation of 1
-- July 2014). The serving or former member, or a dependant, asks: "Am I among
-- those the Navy, Army or Air Force relief fund is for; can I benefit?"

§ `Nouns`

DECLARE `Fund` IS ONE OF
    `the Royal Australian Navy Relief Trust Fund`
    `the Australian Military Forces Relief Trust Fund`
    `the Royal Australian Air Force Welfare Trust Fund`

-- s 4 member of the Defence Force: the person in whose right I apply.
DECLARE `Member` IS ONE OF
    `a member of the Navy, Army or Air Force`
    `a member of a nursing or women's service attached or auxiliary to the Defence Force`
    `a member of a Navy ship's canteen staff`
    `a person accredited to the Defence Force who served officially on full-time paid duty`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Arm` IS ONE OF
    `the Navy`
    `the Army`
    `the Air Force`

DECLARE `Fund case` HAS
    `the fund`                                              IS A `Fund`
    `the member`                                            IS A `Member`
    -- ss 26, 29, 32: "served in, or in association with"
    `the arm the member served in or with`                  IS A `Arm`
    `I am the member`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 4 dependant: in the trustees' opinion
    `the trustees consider me a dependant of the member`    IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 14
    `I am a trustee of the fund or a trustee's dependant`   IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Fund position` HAS
    `I am within the class the fund serves`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am barred from benefiting`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `whether and how much is for the trustees`              IS A BOOLEAN

§ `Rules`

-- ss 26, 29, 32: each fund serves those who served in, or in association with,
-- its arm.
@ref ss 26, 29, 32
GIVEN c IS A `Fund case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arm matches the fund` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `the fund`
    WHEN `the Royal Australian Navy Relief Trust Fund` THEN c's `the arm the member served in or with` EQUALS `the Navy`
    WHEN `the Australian Military Forces Relief Trust Fund` THEN c's `the arm the member served in or with` EQUALS `the Army`
    WHEN `the Royal Australian Air Force Welfare Trust Fund` THEN c's `the arm the member served in or with` EQUALS `the Air Force`

-- s 4 member of the Defence Force and dependant; ss 26, 29, 32.
@ref ss 4, 26, 29, 32
GIVEN c IS A `Fund case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am within the class` c IF
        NOT (c's `the member` EQUALS `none of these`)
    AND `the arm matches the fund` c
    AND (c's `I am the member` OR c's `the trustees consider me a dependant of the member`)

-- s 14: a trustee or a trustee's dependant shall not receive benefits.
@ref s 14
GIVEN c IS A `Fund case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am barred` c IF c's `I am a trustee of the fund or a trustee's dependant`

@ref ss 4, 8, 14, 26, 29, 32
@export default The position of a serving or former member of the Defence Force, or a dependant, under the Services Trust Funds Act 1947 (Cth): whether they are within the class the Royal Australian Navy Relief Trust Fund, the Australian Military Forces Relief Trust Fund or the Royal Australian Air Force Welfare Trust Fund serves (members, including nursing and women's services, canteen staff and accredited officials, who served in or with that arm, and those the trustees consider their dependants: ss 4, 26, 29, 32); whether they are barred as a trustee or a trustee's dependant (s 14); and that whether, and how much, they receive is for the trustees (s 8(a)). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Fund case`  @desc The fund, the member and the arm served in, whether I am the member or a dependant, and whether I am a trustee
GIVETH A `Fund position`
`the fund position for` c MEANS
    `Fund position` OF `I am within the class` c, `I am barred` c, `I am within the class` c AND NOT (`I am barred` c)
